  "behavior": [
    "Both native casing entry paths use one forbidunsafe engine over sealed original-heap payload leases. R single-scalar upper/lower tables replace full Rust Unicode expansions and the old ASCII-only lower-level implementation; no contextual final-sigma rewrite.",
    "Preserve missing strings, declared UTF8 and Native tags, GNU CP1252 interpretation of declared Latin1 (including literal <xx> escapes for its five undefined bytes), names/dim/dimnames/class/custom attributes, object and formal-S4 bits. Shallow-copy the attribute spine and share original values.",
    "Output workspaces count mapped bytes before allocation, admit the complete copy, reconcile actual Vec capacity and retain the original heap ticket through character publication and teardown. Empty copies require no ticket. No CString or uncharged into-String escape.",
    "Managed native boundaries pin/select original arguments and propagate recoverable errors and callback panics. Restore GNU R wrappers for tolower/toupper/casefold: public coercion dispatches as.character methods while internal primitives reject non-character arguments."
  ],
